<title>USA: News Corp eyes Intl Family stake - USA Today.</title>
<headline>News Corp eyes Intl Family stake - USA Today.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>News Corp is seeking to buy about 40 percent of International Family Entertainment Inc and air shows from his Fox Kids service on that company's Family Channel, USA Today said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The paper said News Corp Chief Executive Officer Rupert Murdoch might have to pay about $600 million for the stake. General Electric Co's NBC also remained interested in International Family, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>Neither International Family nor News Corp's U.S. offices were immediately available to comment.</p>
